  "ai_coach": {
    "name": "AI Coach & Automated Guidance",
    "level": "parent",
    "parent_id": null,
    "watch_category": true,
    "watch_reason": "~5.6% of sample volume for the parent overall, but ai_autonomy specifically \u2014 the sharpest complaint shape (\"I can't turn this off\") \u2014 is extremely thin: a full-dataset keyword check (see taxonomy_changelog.md, v2 Fix 1) found exactly one review in all 3,295 describing a user disabling the AI Coach and having it silently re-enable itself. It's kept as its own subcategory anyway, per the brief's instruction not to bury low-volume/ high-stakes signal, but \"watch\" here means \"watch for more examples,\" not \"confirmed at scale.\""
  },
